# No blank white bottle images (North Lane Pick)

**Owner rule 2026-09-02.** Applies to **blog covers** and **Pinterest pin images**.

## Forbidden
- All-white / monochrome plain bottles, tubes, or jars with **no design, color, or label character**
- Sterile “generic white tube + white jar on white vanity” AI still-lifes
- Prompt language that forces: `plain white unbranded tube`, `matte white bottles only`, `no color on packaging`

## Required instead
- Colored glass or packaging (amber, tinted, frosted with tone, pump with visible color)
- Visual depth: material contrast; product surfaces that are not blank pure white

## Backgrounds are fine
Clean vanity / bathroom / marble counters like earlier posts are OK.
Do **not** reject an image only because the backdrop is bright or minimal — reject only blank white *products*.

## Scope
- New blog covers from this date
- New Pinterest pins from this date
- Do not mass-rewrite old posts unless the owner asks
